<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="https://w3id.org/desmos/"
     xml:base="https://w3id.org/desmos/"
     xmlns:crm="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:prov="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
     xmlns:intro="https://w3id.org/lso/intro/beta202506#"
     xmlns:lrmoo="http://iflastandards.info/ns/lrm/lrmoo/"
     xmlns:schema="http://schema.org/"
     xmlns:desmos="https://w3id.org/desmos/"
     xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="https://w3id.org/desmos/">
        <owl:versionIRI rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/desmos/v2.0.0"/>
        <dcterms:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0009-0007-5620-3834"/>
        <dcterms:title xml:lang="en">DeSMòS (Descriptive Semantic Model for Structured Texts)</dcterms:title>
        <dcterms:title xml:lang="it">DeSMòS (Descriptive Semantic Model for Structured Texts)</dcterms:title>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">DeSMòS</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="it">DeSMòS</rdfs:label>
        <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">DeSMòS, Descriptive Semantic Model for Structured Texts, is an OWL 2 ontology for the formal description of literary constraints as text-generative procedures, with particular reference to the Oulipian tradition and its continuation in the Oplepo. The model distinguishes the constraint from the bibliographic entities of the work and its manifestations, represented through LRMoo, and asserts its conceptual autonomy, rather than reducing it to an a posteriori stylistic descriptor attributed to the text. The constraint is linked to the textual production event, in which it guides the creative process; this active role finds a characterizing manifestation in constrained rewriting, where the relationships between source text and resulting text are qualified alongside the textual passages involved. The procedure is characterized according to its formal, semantic, or visual nature, the constrained units, the procedural operations, and its origin, by means of SKOS controlled vocabularies. Its application in the work is documented through intratextual evidence represented via DeSMòS and Genettian paratextual statements, whether epitextual or peritextual, represented through CIDOC CRM and attributable to their authors via PROV-O. DeSMòS supports the documentation, comparative analysis, and SPARQL querying of constrained writing practices across heterogeneous corpora and is aligned with CIDOC CRM, LRMoo, PROV-O, SKOS, INTRO, Dublin Core Terms and Schema.org</dcterms:description>
        <dcterms:description xml:lang="it">DeSMòS, Descriptive Semantic Model for Structured Texts, è un'ontologia OWL 2 per la descrizione formale delle costrizioni letterarie come procedure generative del testo, con particolare riferimento alla tradizione oulipiana e alla sua prosecuzione nell'Oplepo. Il modello distingue la costrizione dalle entità bibliografiche dell'opera e delle sue realizzazioni, rappresentate mediante LRMoo, e ne afferma l'autonomia concettuale, non riducendola ad un descrittore stilistico attribuito a posteriori al testo. La costrizione è collegata all'evento di produzione testuale, nel quale orienta il processo creativo; questo ruolo attivo trova una manifestazione caratterizzante nella riscrittura vincolata, in cui i rapporti fra testo sorgente e testo risultante sono qualificati insieme ai passaggi testuali coinvolti. La procedura è caratterizzata secondo la natura formale, semantica o visiva, le unità vincolate, le operazioni procedurali e l'origine, mediante vocabolari controllati SKOS. Il suo impiego nell'opera è documentato attraverso evidenze intratestuali rappresentate mediante DeSMòS e dichiarazioni paratestuali genettiane, epitestuali o peritestuali, rappresentate mediante CIDOC CRM e attribuibili ai loro autori attraverso PROV-O. DeSMòS supporta la documentazione, l'analisi comparativa e l'interrogazione SPARQL delle pratiche di scrittura vincolata su corpora eterogenei ed è allineata con CIDOC CRM, LRMoo, PROV-O, SKOS, INTRO, Dublin Core Terms e Schema.org</dcterms:description>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">DeSMòS adopts an "alignment-by-reference" pattern to keep the ontology lightweight and reasoner-friendly.</rdfs:comment>
         <rdfs:comment xml:lang="it">DeSMòS adotta un pattern di "allineamento per riferimento" per mantenere l'ontologia leggera e compatibile con i reasoner.</rdfs:comment>
        <dcterms:hasVersion>2.0.0</dcterms:hasVersion>
        <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
        <dcterms:modified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-17</dcterms:modified>
        <dcterms:source rdf:resource="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"/>
        <dcterms:source rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/"/>
        <dcterms:source rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"/>
        <dcterms:source rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#"/>
        <dcterms:source rdf:resource="http://iflastandards.info/ns/lrm/lrmoo/"/>
        <dcterms:source rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/lso/intro/beta202506#"/>
        <dcterms:source rdf:resource="http://schema.org/"/>
        <owl:priorVersion rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/desmos/v1.1.0"/>
        <owl:versionInfo xml:lang="en">Version 2.0.0</owl:versionInfo>
        <owl:versionInfo xml:lang="it">Versione 2.0.0</owl:versionInfo>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


